","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":3240950060,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMjQwOTUwMDYw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/performance","name":"performance","color":"447777","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2025-03-03T10:27:09Z","updated_at":"2025-03-04T22:24:48Z","closed_at":"2025-03-04T22:23:58Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.4.rc3\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.rc3 - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6636) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-6700K CPU @ 4.00GHz (8 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nThis is related to [#3144](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/3144)\n\nThis issue has been there forever and yet still not fixed. When app first starts, it compiles various cache, etc. During that time, depending on your computer, the app may go into not-responding state, which is very unprofessional and might leave a bad taste in users' mouth when they first launch your game.\n\nThe solution to this is to open the window only when it's ready to show your scene, after loading all the subsystems.\nThe window should also not appear in the taskbar until the engine is done loading. This should also fix the no-icon effect when window opens.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3f51c64f-e2ab-4d60-ae9d-7988413e8ed4)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nN/A\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubuserconte